{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions","id":337310,"title":"Bale Hounds and Uratha traditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-11T12:27:36-08:00","id":337310,"title":"Bale Hounds and Uratha traditions","content":"I run a game set in Sweden, when PCs pack is fighting with Bale Hounds pack over small town on the border of Lapland. PCs pack Alpha is very dominating one Rahu ( he would have a Challanger Blood archetype, I so pose - now he have Vice of Dominance ) and he want's to fight with Bale Hounds pack Alpha in the duel. Bale Hounds are ruled by Hound of Rage, Irraka finest hunter known as Olle Erickson.<br /> <br /> Question is this: <b>Would Bale Hounds work under the traditions of Forsaken?</b> Should Olle answer to the duel? Would not he cheat, especially as Rahu have superior physical power and very powerful Fetishes?<br /> <br /> Side question - I have a Hound of Pride, Fang of Fear, that is not sure if he ever was human, terrifying mortals with his wild Urhan and Urshul forms. I will probably run him as Urhanu ( wolf based werewolves from last 2ed spoler ). Question is this - <b>Should I change places him with Olle, so Fang would be Hound of Rage, and Olle the Hound of Pride?</b><br /> <br /> To better show PC character worldview I will post a Blood archetype here from 2ed spoiler.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Challenger</b> \u2013 A Challenger never settles with second place. When things look bleak for the Challenger, he steps up his game. For Uratha, this means overwhelming force. Uratha dominate on the hunt, so the hunt is a tool in the Challenger\u2019s pursuit of victory. Your character recovers a point of Willpower when he ignores safety and reason to look superior. He recovers all Willpower points when he uses Kuruth or the hunt to dominate a rival. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-11-2014, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:15:31-08:00","id":337360,"title":"","content":"I wonder why you keep asking questions that you as the storyteller should answer yourself. It's your game. The Bale Hound Rahu does whatever you need him to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:27:25-08:00","id":337370,"title":"","content":"There is some canon of anagonists, there are some typical answers in supplement. On the reaction to the Bale Hounds, there are not. Also, is they cultivate a Forsaken culture at large. Things like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:40:24-08:00","id":337376,"title":"","content":"The needs of your game matter more than random forumite opinions. Decide these things for yourself; your game will be the better for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T14:58:28-08:00","id":337435,"title":"","content":"Using canon, there's three entirely different kinds of Bale Hounds who would react to it differently.<br /> <br /> But as is the case in all of World of Darkness, whatever the splat it's going to depend on the person, and what their beliefs are regarding honor and how they want to present themselves to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T15:25:38-08:00","id":337448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions?p=337360#post337360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why you keep asking questions that you as the storyteller should answer yourself. It's your game. The Bale Hound Rahu does whatever you need him to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't have put it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T15:56:34-08:00","id":337469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions#post337310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question is this: <b>Would Bale Hounds work under the traditions of Forsaken?</b> Should Olle answer to the duel? Would not he cheat, especially as Rahu have superior physical power and very powerful Fetishes?</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as a hint of a challenge comes up, the Rahu simply attacks and continues until the other Uratha is dead. Full fury. Cheating and using underhanded tactics doesn't really strike me as something a Rahu would do naturally. Sneaky is not their style but more of having the other person throw into a sudden death match as soon that the Rahu hears a change in vocal tones that shows the other person isn't 100% behind the Rahu.<br /> <br /> Also something to mention is that using silver is perfectly viable. As in opening carrying silver weaponry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 12-11-2014, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:19:13-08:00","id":337690,"title":"","content":"Like everyone else said, your game, your decisions, etc. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't see why a the Bale Hound wouldn't cheat, since they don't have much of a code of honor. The only exception would be that, if he served the Maeljin of pride, he might be too proud to cheat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4473-modestmoussorgsky","name":"ModestMoussorgsky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T21:42:18-08:00","id":337715,"title":"","content":"First off, there is confussion on Bale Hounds Alpha persona - probably from my poor wording. Leader of Hounds is <u>Irraka</u>, Hound of Rage - <i>Olle Erricson</i>, locacl great hunter - the Rahu is ( at least for now ) Hound of Pride, coming from wolf who become werewolf.<br /> <br /> On PCs side, Rahu is challangeing player. So duel would be between <b>PC Rahu and Bale Hounds Irraka</b>.<br /> <br /> My <b>second</b> question is: Should ( inside the Bale Hounds pack ) Irraka and Rahu ( Urhanu, wolf based one ) switch with their patrons - so Bale Hounds Alpha would become Hound of Pride and Rahu of Bale Hounds would become Hound of Rage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions?p=337469#post337469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as a hint of a challenge comes up, the Rahu simply attacks and continues until the other Uratha is dead. Full fury. Cheating and using underhanded tactics doesn't really strike me as something a Rahu would do naturally. Sneaky is not their style but more of having the other person throw into a sudden death match as soon that the Rahu hears a change in vocal tones that shows the other person isn't 100% behind the Rahu.<br /> <br /> Also something to mention is that using silver is perfectly viable. As in opening carrying silver weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Bale Hounds are totally non-honorable? Could they even use classical Gifts then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ModestMoussorgsky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions?p=337690#post337690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I don't see why a the Bale Hound wouldn't cheat, since they don't have much of a code of honor. The only exception would be that, if he served the Maeljin of pride, he might be too proud to cheat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point with Hound of Pride here, working with honor only because he is that prideful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> / And this is why I make those topics - I can look on subject from different perspectives and many users recall me info I overlooked in supplements <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T23:01:41-08:00","id":338760,"title":"","content":"Make him a bale hound of violence. Watch that unfold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T23:43:12-08:00","id":338773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions?p=338760#post338760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make him a bale hound of violence. Watch that unfold.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not any Bale Hounds of Violence. There are Hounds of Rage, as their patron is ( looks in White Wolf Wikia for weird name )...<br /> <br /> Oh, you were right, official name of this patron is <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Thurifuge?veaction=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">Thurifuge</a>, Architect of Violence. I still just more like to use Binsfeld's names of Maeljin from <b>WoD: Infero:</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucifer\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a>: pride</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mammon\" target=\"_blank\">Mammon</a>: greed</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmodeus\" target=\"_blank\">Asmodeus</a>: lust</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leviathan\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan</a>: envy</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beelzebub\" target=\"_blank\">Beelzebub</a>: gluttony</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satan\" target=\"_blank\">Satan</a>: wrath</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belphegor\" target=\"_blank\">Belphegor</a>: slot</li> </ul><br /> So Olle is following Satan and the Fang of Fear is supporter of Lucifer. Violance lead Irraka and Pride/Fear lead Rahu could be really interesting combination, come to think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T09:51:15-08:00","id":339165,"title":"","content":"That's cute. The Maeljin are 9 spirits actually.<br /> <br /> Carnala, Lady of Lust<br /> Mammon, Feeder of Greed<br /> Maastraac, Master of Envy<br /> Baalphegor, King of Gluttony<br /> Lamashtu, Calipha of Pride<br /> Beliar, Slave to Sloth<br /> Asmodai, Queen of Wrath<br /> Pseulak, Minister of Deception<br /> Thurifuge, Architect of Violence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T10:19:51-08:00","id":339196,"title":"","content":"Yeajh, I know - but started game with only 7 Hounds as second-in-command and right paw of Alpha is the protestant pastor, Hound of Envy. He, literally, believes they should bring Hell on Earth. So I omitted Pseulak and Thurifuge, at least in this Bale Hounds pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T15:26:10-08:00","id":339482,"title":"","content":"Shame. Those are pretty much the best ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:22:12-08:00","id":339833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/337310-bale-hounds-and-uratha-traditions?p=339482#post339482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shame. Those are pretty much the best ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you say why? I did not see in them anything truly unique or cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:05:20-08:00","id":340181,"title":"","content":"Well I won't speak for Ephsy, they might have their own reasons for liking Pseulak and Thurifuge. I think they're the most interesting because they're not associated with the vices. They're more primordial than that and the reasons behind why they're members of a BBEG group like the maeljin is not obvious at first blush. <br /> <br /> According to legend Thurifuge was just a little violence spirit back in the day before the similarly legendary patricide of Father Wolf, an act so violent that is elevated him through the spirit ranks at an unprecedented rate. Supposedly it also opened the First Wound and some of his greatest agents are direct parodies of Father Wolf. He has far and above the strongest connection to the Uratha in the loose canon of mythology. He's much more personal for a werewolf chronicle. He's also the most powerful of the Maeljin, so more insult to injury that fables lay responsibility for his current existence at the feet of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Pseulak lacks the lore, but makes up for it with being just incredibly insidious. In my own head canon they're a fallen Irralunim and the source of the various moon-related gifts that Bale hounds get, but that's neither here nor there. Unlike Violence that gets some overlap with Wrath, Deception isn't really something any of the other Maeljin can lay a strong claim to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T15:50:59-08:00","id":340264,"title":"","content":"Therifuge is the craft-thing of world-wide conflict, having ascended to Godhood with the death of Urfarah. His personal realm is said to be a palace formed by the Celestine's very bones. His predilect spirit agents are foul mockeries of the shape of Father Wolf Himself, with jaws that resemble saws rather than teeth.<br /> <br /> The Hounds of deception could bring about such intrigue that they could singlehandedly bring about the collapse of individual, pack, or protectorate. My favorite antagonist was one, an Irraka who passed himself for a wolfblood, impregnated female alphas, stuck around just enough to see the beta executed for the crime and had his Maeltinent totem, his own ancestor spirit, control the resulting Unihar. He had a freaking pack of unihar doing his bidding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}